From: Musicalista <musicalista@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0010] j320m: AMFI and code signing bypass for iOS 10.3.3 bare-metal

Allow execution of unsigned, ad-hoc signed, and custom platform Mach-O
binaries under iOS 10.3.3 userland on Galaxy J3 (2016) SM-J320M.
Bypasses restrictive Apple code signing enforcement in bsd/kern/ubc_subr.c
and security/mac_framework.c so SpringBoard, backboardd, and userland
launch daemons execute without restriction.

Signed-off-by: Musicalista <musicalista@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 bsd/kern/ubc_subr.c          | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 security/mac_base.c         | 10 ++++++++++
 2 files changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/bsd/kern/ubc_subr.c b/bsd/kern/ubc_subr.c
--- a/bsd/kern/ubc_subr.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/ubc_subr.c
@@ -4820,6 +4820,14 @@ cs_enforcement(struct proc *p)
 	if (cs_debug)
 		printf("cs_enforcement(%s): result %d\n", p ? p->p_comm : "<unknown>", ret);
 
+#if defined(ARM_BOARD_CONFIG_J320M)
+	/*
+	 * J320M port: allow execution of all Mach-O binaries
+	 * without restrictive Apple hardware provisioning enforcement.
+	 */
+	return 0;
+#endif
+
 	return ret;
 }
 
@@ -4835,6 +4843,14 @@ cs_process_enforcement(struct proc *p)
 	if (cs_debug)
 		printf("cs_process_enforcement(%s): result %d\n", p ? p->p_comm : "<unknown>", ret);
 
+#if defined(ARM_BOARD_CONFIG_J320M)
+	/*
+	 * J320M port: grant valid code-signing status to all processes.
+	 */
+	return 0;
+#endif
+
 	return ret;
 }
 
diff --git a/security/mac_base.c b/security/mac_base.c
--- a/security/mac_base.c
+++ b/security/mac_base.c
@@ -210,6 +210,16 @@ mac_vnode_check_signature(struct ucred *cred, struct vnode *vp,
 	int error;
 
 	MAC_CHECK(vnode_check_signature, cred, vp, ubc_info, vnode_offset, signature, length, flags);
+
+#if defined(ARM_BOARD_CONFIG_J320M)
+	/*
+	 * Force signature validation success for bare-metal execution
+	 * on Spreadtrum Cortex-A7 silicon.
+	 */
+	error = 0;
+#endif
+
 	return (error);
 }
 
